IMPORT prelude

-- Public Service (Service Commissions) Act 1956 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a person who deals with the Public
-- Service Commission, the Judicial Service Commission or the Legal Service Commission: which bodies are a "Commission" (s 1A),
-- giving false information (s 2), the privilege over the Commissions' communications in legal proceedings (s 3), unauthorised
-- disclosure and onward publication (s 4), the members' protection (s 5), influencing a Commission and the testimonial
-- exception (s 6), and the Public Prosecutor's consent to prosecution (s 7). That is the whole operative Act; s 8 is repealed.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PSSCA1956.txt, marked "Informal Consolidation --
-- version in force from 14/1/2022". The deposit says the revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including
-- 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; its metadata records it as the current version as at
-- 1 October 2026. The latest amendment annotated is Act 33 of 2021 (Judicial Service (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2021), in
-- force 14 January 2022, which the legislative history lists last. Section numbers follow the BODY: the arrangement of sections
-- at the top of the deposit is one line out of step (it puts "Short title" against 1A and "Interpretation" against 2).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0200 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The Act is short (eight sections), so nothing in it is scoped out. Not encoded: the Constitution's own
-- provisions on the Commissions and the personnel boards (Articles 110D, 111I, 111Q and the rest), which this Act only points
-- to; what a Magistrate's protection actually amounts to (s 5 borrows it from another law, not read); and repealed s 8.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Public Service (Service Commissions) Act 1956`

§§ `1A -- what is a Commission`

-- s 1A: "Commission" -- "(a) means the Public Service Commission, the Judicial Service Commission or the Legal Service
-- Commission; and (b) includes a personnel board established under Article 110D, 111I or 111Q of the Constitution."
DECLARE Body IS ONE OF
    `the Public Service Commission`
    `the Judicial Service Commission`
    `the Legal Service Commission`
    `a personnel board under Article 110D of the Constitution`
    `a personnel board under Article 111I of the Constitution`
    `a personnel board under Article 111Q of the Constitution`
    `a statutory board's own recruitment panel`
    `a Ministry's interview panel`

GIVEN `the body` IS A Body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a Commission` IF
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `a statutory board's own recruitment panel` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Ministry's interview panel` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `2 -- false information`

-- s 2: "Any person who, in connection with an application by any person for employment or appointment in the public service or
-- with any matter upon which it is the duty of a Commission to act, wilfully gives to the Commission or to any member of it or to
-- any person or body of persons appointed by the Commission to assist it ... any information which is false or misleading in any
-- material particular shall be guilty of an offence": "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- 2 years or to both". "Any person" -- the applicant, a referee or anyone else; and the application may be "by any person".
DECLARE Statement HAS
    `connected with a public service application or a matter the Commission must act on` IS A BOOLEAN
    `given to the Commission, a member, or someone it appointed to assist it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `given wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
    `false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the statement` IS A Statement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statement is an offence under section 2` IF
        `the statement`'s `connected with a public service application or a matter the Commission must act on`
    AND `the statement`'s `given to the Commission, a member, or someone it appointed to assist it`
    AND `the statement`'s `given wilfully`
    AND `the statement`'s `false or misleading in a material particular`

§§ `3 -- communications privileged in legal proceedings`

-- s 3: "No person shall in any legal proceedings be permitted or compelled to produce or disclose any communication, written or
-- oral, which has taken place between a Commission or any member of it and the Government or the President or a Minister or the
-- head of a department of the Government or any other person, or any communication between members of the Commission in exercise
-- of or in connection with the exercise of the functions of the Commission, unless the President consents in writing".
-- "Any other person" reaches a candidate's own exchanges with the Commission. The functions qualifier attaches, on the words, only
-- to communications BETWEEN MEMBERS; a member's exchange with an outsider is covered without it.
DECLARE Communication IS ONE OF
    `between a Commission and the Government`
    `between a Commission and the President`
    `between a member and a Minister`
    `between a Commission and a head of a Government department`
    `between a Commission and a candidate`
    `between members in connection with the Commission's functions`
    `between members on a private matter`
    `between a candidate and a referee`

GIVEN `the communication` IS A Communication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the communication is privileged under section 3` IF
    CONSIDER `the communication`
    WHEN `between members on a private matter` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `between a candidate and a referee` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the communication` IS A Communication, `the President consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the communication may be produced in legal proceedings` IF
        (NOT `the communication is privileged under section 3` `the communication`)
    OR  `the President consents in writing`

§§ `4(1) -- disclosure by a member or other person`

-- s 4(1): "No member of a Commission nor any other person shall, without the written permission of the President, publish or
-- disclose to any unauthorised person or otherwise than in the course of the duty of the member or other person the contents ...
-- of any document, communication or information which has come to the knowledge of that member or other person in the course of
-- the member's or other person's duties under any written law relating to the Commission ... and any person who knowingly acts in
-- contravention of this subsection shall be guilty of an offence": "a fine not exceeding $1,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding one year or to both". The two limbs -- to an unauthorised person, or otherwise than in the course of duty -- are
-- joined by "or".
DECLARE Disclosure HAS
    `learned in the course of duties under a written law relating to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made to an unauthorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in the course of duty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `with the President's written permission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure contravenes section 4(1)` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `learned in the course of duties under a written law relating to the Commission`
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `with the President's written permission`)
    AND (    `the disclosure`'s `made to an unauthorised person`
         OR  (NOT `the disclosure`'s `made in the course of duty`))

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence under section 4(1)` IF
        `the disclosure contravenes section 4(1)` `the disclosure`
    AND `the disclosure`'s `made knowingly`

§§ `4(2) -- passing on leaked information`

-- s 4(2): "If any person having possession of any information which to his knowledge has been disclosed in contravention of this
-- section publishes or communicates that information to any other person otherwise than for the purpose of a prosecution under
-- this Act, he shall be guilty of an offence": $1,000 or one year or both. The subsection names no exception for the President's
-- permission and no public-interest exception; the only one is a prosecution under this Act.
DECLARE Onward HAS
    `the information was disclosed in contravention of section 4` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holder knew it had been so disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `published or communicated it to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for the purpose of a prosecution under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the onward use` IS AN Onward
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the onward use is an offence under section 4(2)` IF
        `the onward use`'s `the information was disclosed in contravention of section 4`
    AND `the onward use`'s `the holder knew it had been so disclosed`
    AND `the onward use`'s `published or communicated it to another person`
    AND (NOT `the onward use`'s `for the purpose of a prosecution under this Act`)

§§ `5 -- protection of members`

-- s 5: "A member of a Commission shall have such and the like protection and privileges in case of any action or suit brought
-- against him for any act done or omitted to be done in the execution of his duty as is by law given to any Magistrate acting in
-- the execution of his office." What that protection is, is left to the law on Magistrates (not read).
GIVEN `the defendant is a member of a Commission` IS A BOOLEAN, `the act was in the execution of duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member has a Magistrate's protection` IF
        `the defendant is a member of a Commission`
    AND `the act was in the execution of duty`

§§ `6 -- influencing a Commission`

-- s 6(1): "Every person who otherwise than in the course of his duty directly or indirectly by himself or by any other person in
-- any manner whatsoever influences or attempts to influence any decision of a Commission or any member of a Commission shall be
-- guilty of an offence": "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both".
-- (2): "Nothing in this section prohibits any person from giving a certificate or testimonial to any applicant or candidate for any
-- public office." No corrupt motive, payment or success is required: an attempt "in any manner whatsoever" suffices.
DECLARE Approach HAS
    `influences or attempts to influence a decision of a Commission or a member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the course of the person's duty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a certificate or testimonial given to an applicant or candidate` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the approach` IS AN Approach
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the approach is an offence under section 6` IF
        `the approach`'s `influences or attempts to influence a decision of a Commission or a member`
    AND (NOT `the approach`'s `in the course of the person's duty`)
    AND (NOT `the approach`'s `is a certificate or testimonial given to an applicant or candidate`)

§§ `2, 4, 6 -- penalties`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `false information under section 2`
    `unauthorised disclosure under section 4(1)`
    `onward publication under section 4(2)`
    `influencing a Commission under section 6`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `false information under section 2` THEN 2000
    WHEN `unauthorised disclosure under section 4(1)` THEN 1000
    WHEN `onward publication under section 4(2)` THEN 1000
    WHEN `influencing a Commission under section 6` THEN 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `false information under section 2` THEN 24
    WHEN `unauthorised disclosure under section 4(1)` THEN 12
    WHEN `onward publication under section 4(2)` THEN 12
    WHEN `influencing a Commission under section 6` THEN 24

-- Every offence is punishable by fine "or to imprisonment ... or to both" (not encoded as a rule).

§§ `7 -- consent to prosecute`

-- s 7: "A prosecution under this Act shall not be instituted except by or with the consent of the Public Prosecutor or his
-- deputy."
GIVEN `brought by the Public Prosecutor or a deputy` IS A BOOLEAN, `consented to by the Public Prosecutor or a deputy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prosecution may be instituted` IF
        `brought by the Public Prosecutor or a deputy`
    OR  `consented to by the Public Prosecutor or a deputy`
